---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
import { APP_NAME, LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE, PRIVACY_EMAIL, PUBLISHER } from '../data/site';

interface DeclaredData {
  category: string;
  types: string;
  source: string;
  purposes: string;
  processor: string;
}

const DECLARED: readonly DeclaredData[] = [
  {
    category: 'User content',
    types: 'Photos or videos, audio data',
    source: 'Videos you trace with the app',
    purposes: 'App functionality; improving our algorithms',
    processor: 'Google Firebase (Cloud Storage)',
  },
  {
    category: 'User content',
    types: 'Customer support messages',
    source: 'The feedback form in the app, only if you send it',
    purposes: 'App functionality (answering you)',
    processor: 'Formspree',
  },
  {
    category: 'Contact info',
    types: 'Name (optional), email address',
    source: 'The feedback form in the app, only if you send it',
    purposes: 'App functionality (answering you)',
    processor: 'Formspree',
  },
  {
    category: 'Identifiers',
    types: 'User ID',
    source: 'The anonymous account the app creates for you',
    purposes: 'App functionality; analytics',
    processor: 'Google Firebase, Mixpanel, Adapty, Firebase Crashlytics, Formspree',
  },
  {
    category: 'Identifiers',
    types: 'Device ID',
    source: 'Firebase installation ID, Mixpanel device ID, the vendor identifier read by Adapty',
    purposes: 'App functionality; analytics',
    processor: 'Google Firebase, Mixpanel, Adapty',
  },
  {
    category: 'Purchases',
    types: 'Purchase history',
    source: 'Your subscription and its transactions',
    purposes: 'App functionality (selling and restoring your subscription); analytics',
    processor: 'Adapty and the App Store; Adapty forwards purchase events to Mixpanel',
  },
  {
    category: 'Usage data',
    types: 'Product interaction',
    source: 'App usage events (screens, buttons, editor settings, export results, paywall views, errors)',
    purposes: 'Analytics',
    processor: 'Mixpanel',
  },
  {
    category: 'Location',
    types: 'Coarse location (city, region, country)',
    source: 'Derived by Mixpanel from your IP address',
    purposes: 'Analytics',
    processor: 'Mixpanel',
  },
  {
    category: 'Diagnostics',
    types: 'Crash data, other diagnostic data',
    source: 'Crash reports, recorded errors and log lines; error events',
    purposes: 'App functionality (finding and fixing problems); analytics',
    processor: 'Firebase Crashlytics, Mixpanel',
  },
];
---
<ContentPage
  pageTitle={`Privacy Policy · ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`What ${APP_NAME} collects, why, who receives it, and what you can do about it.`}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p><strong>Effective date: {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</strong></p>
  <p>
    This policy explains what the {APP_NAME} iOS app ("Tracer", "the app") collects, why, who receives it,
    and what you can do about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Tracer is published by {PUBLISHER} ("we", "us"). We decide how your data is used, so we are the data controller.
    Contact: <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You do not create a login. The app gives you an anonymous account with a random user ID.</li>
    <li>Videos you trace with the app may be used to improve our algorithms.</li>
    <li>We use Mixpanel for app analytics, Google Firebase for the app backend and Firebase Crashlytics for crash reports, Adapty for subscriptions, and Formspree for the feedback form.</li>
    <li><strong>We do not sell your data.</strong> We do not show ads. <strong>We do not track you</strong> across other companies' apps or websites.</li>
    <li>You can delete your account in the app, and ask us by email to delete everything else.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your account is anonymous</h2>
  <p>
    When you first open the app, it signs you in to Firebase Authentication as an anonymous user, and Firebase gives
    you a random user ID. We do not ask for your name, email, phone number or Apple ID to use the app.
  </p>
  <p>
    This user ID links your data across our services: videos used to improve our algorithms, analytics events, recorded errors and logs,
    your subscription record and the messages we show you in the app. Crash reports themselves are tied to a
    Firebase installation ID.
  </p>
  <p>
    To find your user ID, open Settings in the app and tap the version number. The app copies your user ID and
    Firebase installation ID to the clipboard. Include them when you write to us so we can find your data.
  </p>

  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The videos you pick to trace, and the projects you make from them (traces, effects, settings).</li>
    <li>Your rendered videos, until you save them to Photos.</li>
    <li>The reminder notification the app schedules after a preview, including its thumbnail.</li>
    <li>Your app preferences.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The app reads only the videos you choose in the iOS photo picker; it does not get access to the rest of your
    photo library. To save a video it asks for add-only access to Photos, which lets it add videos but not read your library.
  </p>

  <h2>Improving our algorithms</h2>
  <p>
    Videos you trace with the app may be used to improve our algorithms, such as the model that finds the ball.
    To have yours removed, delete your account in the app or email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>
    with your user ID.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <p>
    These are the data types we declare in the App Store privacy label. Every type is linked to your anonymous
    user ID, and none is used to track you.
  </p>
  <div class="not-prose flex flex-col gap-3">
    {DECLARED.map((row) => (
      <section class="ss-card flex flex-col gap-2 p-4 text-subhead">
        <span class="ss-tag text-volt">{row.category}</span>
        <h3 class="text-title-3 text-ice">{row.types}</h3>
        <p class="text-mist"><span class="text-ice">From:</span> {row.source}</p>
        <p class="text-mist"><span class="text-ice">Why:</span> {row.purposes}</p>
        <p class="text-mist"><span class="text-ice">Processed by:</span> {row.processor}</p>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p>
    The app also uses the Firebase installation ID and basic device details to deliver app configuration, in-app
    messages and push notifications (only if you allow them), and Apple App Attest through Firebase App Check to
    protect our backend from abuse.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not collect your precise location, contacts, health data, browsing or search history, or advertising identifier (IDFA).
  </p>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>
    The feedback form in the app sends your name (optional), email, message, user ID and app version to Formspree, a form
    service that forwards it to us. The app keeps your name and email on your device to fill in the form next time.
    If you write to us by email instead, your email provider's policy applies to that message.
  </p>

  <h2>Network requests without account data</h2>
  <p>
    The app downloads the ball tracking model from Apple's On-Demand Resources or, as a fallback, from a file host at
    DigitalOcean, and checks the current time with worldtimeapi.org to apply the free export limit. These requests carry
    your IP address and normal request data, but no user ID.
  </p>

  <h2>Who receives your data</h2>
  <p>We use these service providers. Each processes data for us under its own terms.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google Firebase (Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Cloud Storage, Remote Config, Crashlytics, Cloud Messaging, App Check): <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a></li>
    <li>Mixpanel (analytics): <a href="https://mixpanel.com/legal/privacy-policy/">mixpanel.com/legal/privacy-policy</a></li>
    <li>Adapty (subscriptions and paywalls): <a href="https://adapty.io/privacy/">adapty.io/privacy</a></li>
    <li>Apple (App Store purchases, App Attest, push delivery, On-Demand Resources): <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">apple.com/legal/privacy</a></li>
    <li>Formspree (feedback form): <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy</a></li>
    <li>DigitalOcean (model file hosting): <a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/legal/privacy-policy">digitalocean.com/legal/privacy-policy</a></li>
    <li>worldtimeapi.org (time check): <a href="https://worldtimeapi.org">worldtimeapi.org</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose data if the law requires it, to protect our rights or users' safety, or to a buyer if
    {PUBLISHER} or the app is sold.
  </p>

  <h2>No tracking, no selling</h2>
  <p>
    The app does not track you as Apple defines it. It does not read your advertising identifier and does not show the
    App Tracking Transparency prompt. Your data is not combined with data from other companies' apps or websites for
    advertising, and it is not given to data brokers. We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for
    cross-context behavioral advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Videos used to improve our algorithms: until you delete your account or ask us to, or until we no longer need them.</li>
    <li>Analytics events (Mixpanel): until we delete them or you ask us to.</li>
    <li>Crash reports, recorded errors and logs (Firebase Crashlytics): 90 days.</li>
    <li>Subscription records (Adapty): while needed to provide and restore your subscription, and as required for tax and accounting.</li>
    <li>Feedback: until we have handled it, then as long as it is useful for support history.</li>
    <li>Firebase account and in-app messages: until you delete your account.</li>
    <li>Data on your device: until you delete it or the app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>In the app, open Settings and tap "Delete account". The app then:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>deletes the videos this phone sent us under your current account;</li>
    <li>deletes your Firestore records (your in-app messages and their read state);</li>
    <li>deletes your anonymous Firebase account;</li>
    <li>deletes your projects and their videos on this device, your saved feedback name and email, and other per-account settings;</li>
    <li>creates a new anonymous account.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Deleting your account does not cancel your subscription: manage it in your Apple ID settings, and use
    "Restore purchases" afterwards to use it again.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some data cannot be deleted from the app: Mixpanel analytics, your Adapty subscription profile, Crashlytics reports
    (they expire after 90 days), videos already used to improve our algorithms or sent under an earlier account or
    install, and feedback you sent. To have these deleted, email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>
    with your user ID (copy it before you delete your account). We delete what we can find for that ID within 30 days
    and tell you what was deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to access, correct or delete your data, or to stop using it for analytics or model training. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a> with your user ID; we answer within 30 days. Because accounts
    are anonymous, we use your user ID to find your data and may ask for it to confirm a request.
  </p>
  <h3>EEA, UK and Switzerland</h3>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR and UK GDPR you can access, rectify, erase, restrict and port your data, and object to processing based
    on legitimate interests. We rely on contract for running your account and subscription, on legitimate interests for
    analytics, diagnostics, feedback and improving ball tracking, and on consent for push notifications, which you can
    withdraw in iOS Settings. You can complain to your local data protection authority.
  </p>
  <h3>California and other US states</h3>
  <p>
    You have the right to know what personal information we collect, use and disclose, to delete and correct it, and not
    to be treated differently for using these rights. We do not sell or share personal information, so there is nothing
    to opt out of. In the last 12 months we collected identifiers, commercial information (purchase history), app activity,
    approximate location derived from IP address, audio and visual information (videos you trace) and the name and email
    you give in feedback, and disclosed them only to the service providers above for the purposes above.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Tracer is not directed to children under 13, or under 16 in the EEA and UK, and we do not knowingly collect their data.
    If you believe a child has used the app, email us and we will delete the data for that user ID.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We are based in the United States, and our providers process data in the United States and other countries. For
    transfers from the EEA, UK or Switzerland we rely on safeguards such as the European Commission's Standard Contractual
    Clauses or the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, as offered by each provider.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data travels over encrypted connections. Our Firebase security rules let each anonymous account read and delete only
    its own records and videos. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects you, we will tell you as the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We post changes on this page and update the effective date. If a change materially affects how we use your data,
    we tell you in the app before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{PUBLISHER} · <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a></p>
</ContentPage>
